{
  "hadith_number": 17,
  "text": "On the authority of Abu Yalla, Shadad Ibn Aus, may Allah be pleased with him, that the messenger of Allah, may the blessings and peace of Allah be upon him, said, fairly Allah as prescribed proficiency in all things. Thus, if you kill, kill well, and if you slaughter, slaughter well. Let each one of you sharpen his blade and let him us best suffering to animal he slurses. It was related to Bo Muslim.",
